{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning, Mrs Hale. Blood pressure is one hundred and sixty-four over ninety-six, pulse seventy-eight, and the weight is seventy-nine point four kilos.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. Is that a lot?",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Doctor's on his way in. Your daughter can come through with you.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She's been worried sick about her ankles, that's why I booked us in.",
  "[SEG0005] person_4 (DOCTOR): Swollen ankles?",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Yes, puffy, both of them. Her shoes won't do up.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Well, actually, they just feel tight. I don't know, doctor, I didn't want a fuss.",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (DOCTOR): How long for?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. Claire does the remembering.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Um, two weeks... no, five weeks. Sorry, I misspoke. Five weeks, since we came back from my sister's.",
  "[SEG0011] person_4 (DOCTOR): Aching?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): By the evening, yes, they ache.",
  "[SEG0013] person_4 (DOCTOR): Breathless?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Um, a bit, if I walk through to the kitchen. Not when I'm sitting.",
  "[SEG0015] person_4 (DOCTOR): Chest pain?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (DOCTOR): Cough?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No cough.",
  "[SEG0019] person_4 (DOCTOR): Waking short of breath?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I don't know, doctor, I sleep alright.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She gets up once a night for a wee. That's been ages, not just lately.",
  "[SEG0022] person_4 (DOCTOR): Who sorts the tablets?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I do. I live in. Pill box every Sunday.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (DOCTOR): Go on.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The water tablet. Furosemide. Forty... no, twenty milligrams. I nearly said the old dose. It's twenty, once in the morning.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know the names. There's a little white one as well. Two of them, I think.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (NURSE): Sorry to jump in. The screen has amlodipine down as ten milligrams.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No, the packet at home is five milligrams. One little white tablet, once a day, and she's been counting that same one twice.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Am I? I don't know, doctor. I just swallow what she gives me.",
  "[SEG0030] person_4 (DOCTOR): One amlodipine a day, then. Screen says ten, the packet says five. I'm not changing that today.",
  "[SEG0031] person_4 (DOCTOR): Anything stopped by someone else?",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The hospital doctor stopped bisoprolol, the tiny pink one, about six weeks back, after dizzy turns on the ward. She hasn't had it since.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't remember that. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0034] person_4 (DOCTOR): Anything else in the box?",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ramipril five milligrams at night, for the blood pressure. I give her that one.",
  "[SEG0036] person_4 (DOCTOR): Allergies?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No. Never had a rash or a funny turn with a tablet.",
  "[SEG0039] person_4 (DOCTOR): Ankles and chest, then.",
  "[SEG0040] person_4 (DOCTOR): Mild pitting oedema, both ankles. Chest is clear, no crackles. No murmur.",
  "[SEG0041] person_4 (DOCTOR): Heart failure on the list?",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Mild heart failure, the GP said, last year. Blood pressure for years. Both still there.",
  "[SEG0043] person_4 (DOCTOR): Existing heart failure and hypertension. Fine.",
  "[SEG0044] person_4 (DOCTOR): Smoke?",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (PATIENT): Never. I don't know what else to tell you.",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): A small sherry on a Sunday, that's all. Bungalow, she lives with me. She hardly walks out.",
  "[SEG0047] person_4 (DOCTOR): Twenty of furosemide isn't enough. I'm increasing it to forty milligrams, once every morning, by mouth, for the swelling.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): Forty? I don't know, doctor. They brought it down before.",
  "[SEG0049] person_4 (DOCTOR): They did, and we're putting it back up. Claire, redo the box tonight, one amlodipine only, don't double it. Ramipril stays at five milligrams at night. Bisoprolol stays stopped.",
  "[SEG0050] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I'll sort the box when we get in.",
  "[SEG0051] person_4 (DOCTOR): Kidney bloods and electrolytes. I'm requesting them now.",
  "[SEG0052] person_1 (NURSE): I can bleed her Thursday morning.",
  "[SEG0053] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Thursday's fine, I'll bring her. Traffic was a nightmare getting here, mind.",
  "[SEG0054] person_4 (DOCTOR): I'll see her back here in three weeks. If the swelling is worse before that, or she's breathless sitting still, come sooner.",
  "[SEG0055] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. Is it serious?",
  "[SEG0056] person_4 (DOCTOR): Working impression is fluid from the heart failure, water tablet too low. Chest is clear, so this is not a chest infection.",
  "[SEG0057] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): We'll watch her. Thanks."
 ],
